// Host tests for DanceBudget (B.6's per-move budget, the dirty rule of B.5
// in DanceStage.h, D.2's start-spot hook, the verdict and the one-move-a-
// frame pass): docs/DANCE-SPRITES.md, Appendix E.4's test_dance_budget list,
// item by item. Written from the doc alone, without reading the
// implementation.
//
// - BudgetVectors.h (generated by dancepack.py) pins every case, every
//   move's verdict and one frame trace per move of the fixture; the C++
//   must agree bit for bit.
// - The worked examples are A.17's dot, B.4's move (built here with
//   beatscript::miniPack) and B.5's rects.
// - Packs are exact-size heap copies and the median's scratch an exact-size
//   heap block of kBudgetMaxFrames values, so ASan reports an overrun.
//
// Run: pio test -e native -f test_dance_budget (and native_asan, E.4).
#if defined(DANCE_ASAN) && !defined(__SANITIZE_ADDRESS__)
#error "native_asan: -fsanitize=address didn't reach the compiler (docs/DANCE-SPRITES.md, Appendix D.5)"
#endif

